<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Norodom Ranariddh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1944–2021</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Norodom Ranariddh was a Cambodian prince and politician, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norodom-of-cambodia">King Norodom</a> Sihanouk and leader of the royalist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/funcinpec">FUNCINPEC</a> party. After FUNCINPEC won the UN-supervised elections of 1993 he became first prime minister, sharing power with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hun-sen">Hun Sen</a> as second prime minister. Hun Sen ousted him in armed fighting in July 1997, and he later served as president of the National Assembly.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/norodom-ranariddh.jpg" alt="Norodom Ranariddh" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: His Royal Highness Samdech Krom Preah Norodom Ranariddh · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ranariddh_self_portrait.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
